# Root-anchored (/docs/, not docs/). .vercelignore takes gitignore-style
# patterns, so an unanchored docs/ matches ANY directory of that name at any
# depth - including assets/docs/, which holds the resume the contact section
# links to. That shipped, and the resume 404'd on the live site while being
# present in the repository the whole time.
#
# Working documents, not site content. These were publicly reachable on the
# previous host because it served the repository root verbatim - including the
# case-study notes, which are candid internal critique and not for visitors.
